
  PART 1  THE TWO FACES

  (a) THE CHARGE FACE (G156 ontology, H047 N10, G234-a):
        the species IS the scalar's charge -- the equilibrium phase, the
        sourced field's Gauss-map charge.  No particle scale: lambda_fs = 0
        EXACT, R(k) = P_framework/P_LCDM = 1 at EVERY k, no cut, no break,
        the sub-halo mass function keeps its CDM power-law rise below 1e6
        Msun (dN/dlnM(1e5)/dN/dlnM(1e7) = 63.1).  MEASURED by the census
        (G215): S_meas = 1.0 (no break) at the RAR > 1e5 class, N_obs = 19.
  (b) THE PARTICLE FACE (G212, G234-b):
        the SAME number is a rest mass: m = 5.09 +- 0.10 keV, lambda_fs =
        0.5584 Mpc, k_hm = 57.22 h/Mpc, M_hm = 7.34e+05 Msun (sim-fit) / 8.41e+06
        (window): a WARM CUT, the sub-halo mass function INVERTED below
        ~1e6 Msun, T^2(1e6) = 5e-13.  The 5.09 keV number is the SAME number
        two ways: the equilibrium's phase temperature converted to an energy
        (T_phase = m sigma^2/k_B = T_CMB at z*, G168 -- a temperature does
        NOT free-stream) or a rest mass (which does).

  THE CONTRAST, stated plainly:
        ONE sector cannot both free-stream at 0.558 Mpc and lock at R(k) = 1.
        A 5.09 keV particle carries T^2(k) = [1+(alpha k)^2.24]^-8.93:
        T^2( 10 h/Mpc) = 0.9704  ->  R_particle = 0.9704  (1-R = 0.0296)
        T^2( 30 h/Mpc) = 0.7074  ->  R_particle = 0.7074  (1-R = 0.2926)
        T^2(100 h/Mpc) = 0.0162  ->  R_particle = 0.0162  (1-R = 0.9838)
        T^2(300 h/Mpc) = 0.0000  ->  R_particle = 0.0000  (1-R = 1.0000)
        while the charge face says R = 1 there (1 - R = 0.0000000000): the
        SAME sector loses 31% of its power at k = 30 and 99% at k = 100
        under the particle reading and loses NOTHING under the charge
        reading.  The difference is the ontology of the 5.09 keV number,
        and it is a FACT about the same k-range: the contradiction is real
        for a single-substance sector; it is a TESTABLE two-component
        statement for a two-face sector (Part 2).

  PART 2  THE SCALE SEPARATION HYPOTHESIS: THE COMPOSITE P(k)

  THE HYPOTHESIS: the phantom (the equilibrium charge, R(k) = 1) dominates
  the galaxy/cluster/large scales; the warm dust (lambda_fs = 0.558 Mpc)
  dominates the sub-halo scales.  The composite matter power
        P(k) = P_charge(k) + P_dust(smeared by T_WDM^2)
  i.e. the composite transfer, the power ratio to LCDM:
        R_comp(k; f_d) = (1 - f_d) x 1 + f_d x T^2_WDM(k; m = 5.09),
  with f_d the warm-dust fraction of the dark sector.  The two components
  add in power (uncorrelated, same primordial spectrum): the charge's flat
  plateau at R = 1 rides under the dust's cut at every k; the dust paints
  the break on top of it.

  THE BREAK LADDER at m = 5.09 keV (computed):
        onset   k ~ 1/lambda_fs = 1/0.5584 = 1.79 h/Mpc   (1-T^2 = 6.4e-04)
        1%     k ~ 6.1 h/Mpc;   half-mode k_hm = 57.2 h/Mpc (M_hm = 7.34e+05)
        f_d = 0.9 composite reaches 5% suppression at k ~ 13.3 h/Mpc
        saturation 1 - f_d (the full dust missing) above ~300 h/Mpc

  THE COMPOSITE ON THE GRID (R_comp vs k):
        k [h/Mpc]    T^2(m=5.09)   R(fd=0.9)   R(fd=0.5)   R(fd=0.98)
             0.10       1.0000      1.0000      1.0000      1.0000
             1.00       0.9998      0.9998      0.9999      0.9998
             5.00       0.9936      0.9943      0.9968      0.9938
            10.00       0.9704      0.9733      0.9852      0.9710
            20.00       0.8683      0.8815      0.9341      0.8709
            30.00       0.7074      0.7366      0.8537      0.7132
            57.22       0.2500      0.3250      0.6250      0.2650
           100.00       0.0162      0.1146      0.5081      0.0359
           300.00       0.0000      0.1000      0.5000      0.0200
          1000.00       0.0000      0.1000      0.5000      0.0200
        AT k <= 1 h/Mpc the composite differs from R = 1 by at most 1.7e-04
        (f_d = 1): 1 - R_comp = f_d x 1.7e-04 -- 0.02% suppression at the DES-Y3
        lensing kernel: the LSS/CMB scales are BLIND to the composition.
        AT k ~ 10-60 the break is visible; above ~300 the dust face's cut
        is total and only the charge's plateau (1 - f_d) survives.

  PART 3  THE OBSERVABLE

  (a) THE LYMAN-ALPHA FOREST at k ~ 10-100 h/Mpc (the ladder, G093):
      the composite must not be suppressed more than the weakest allowed
      species at its own confidence level:
      f_d,max(k) = [1 - T^2(k; m_lb)] / [1 - T^2(k; 5.09 keV)]:
        k =    1.0 h/Mpc:  f_d,max = 2.935 (3.3 keV (Viel+13, 2sig))  /  0.904 (5.3 keV (Irsic+17, 2sig))  /  0.754 (5.7 keV (Villasenor+24, 95%, the record))
        k =   10.0 h/Mpc:  f_d,max = 2.844 (3.3 keV (Viel+13, 2sig))  /  0.905 (5.3 keV (Irsic+17, 2sig))  /  0.757 (5.7 keV (Villasenor+24, 95%, the record))
        k =   20.0 h/Mpc:  f_d,max = 2.546 (3.3 keV (Viel+13, 2sig))  /  0.911 (5.3 keV (Irsic+17, 2sig))  /  0.769 (5.7 keV (Villasenor+24, 95%, the record))
        k =   30.0 h/Mpc:  f_d,max = 2.135 (3.3 keV (Viel+13, 2sig))  /  0.920 (5.3 keV (Irsic+17, 2sig))  /  0.789 (5.7 keV (Villasenor+24, 95%, the record))
        k =  100.0 h/Mpc:  f_d,max = 1.016 (3.3 keV (Viel+13, 2sig))  /  0.994 (5.3 keV (Irsic+17, 2sig))  /  0.978 (5.7 keV (Villasenor+24, 95%, the record))
      the BINDING forest constraint is nearly k-INDEPENDENT: f_d < ~0.76-0.79
      across the whole window under the record (5.7 keV, 95%) rung -- the
      ladder's spine excludes a budget-required f_d ~ 0.98 at 95%, and the
      CENSUS is the sharper constraint.

  (b) THE DES-Y3 / CMB lensing at k ~ 1 h/Mpc: 1 - T^2(1) =
      1.7e-04 -- the two faces are indistinguishable at the LSS/CMB scales
      (R = 1 - epsilon for ANY f_d): no dust fraction is constrained there.

  (c) THE SUB-HALO CENSUS (G215) at k ~ 100-500 h/Mpc (M ~ 1e5-1e8 Msun):
      S(1e5; 5.09) = 0.1918 (log-m interpolation of G115's committed rows
      0.0529@3.3 / 0.2688@5.7); pure-5.09 count = 19 x 0.192 = 3.6
      vs N_obs = 19 -> z = -3.52 sigma; the COMPOSITE's index is
      z(f_d) = -3.52 f_d: 1-sigma f_d < 0.28, 2-sigma f_d < 0.57,
      3-sigma f_d < 0.85; at the budget-required f_d = 0.98: z = -3.45.

  (d) THE ONE-PHOTON-SCALE TEST: the Lyman-alpha flux power at the scale of
      ONE absorption (one photon at one velocity width <-> one comoving
      scale, k ~ 5-30 h/Mpc) is the probe whose band coincides with the
      cut's visible onset -- the test that SEES the cut:
        f_d = 0.5: suppression 1 - R_comp = 0.015 @10 / 0.146 @30 h/Mpc
        f_d = 0.9: suppression 1 - R_comp = 0.027 @10 / 0.263 @30 h/Mpc
        f_d = 1.0: suppression 1 - R_comp = 0.030 @10 / 0.293 @30 h/Mpc
      a 10% flux-power measurement at k ~ 30 sees f_d = 0.9 at ~2.6 sigma
      (suppression 0.263); the current 95% bound (m > 5.7 keV) is already
      at this class -- the cut is visible AT the forest's high-k edge, and
      today's data keep it consistent only because 5.09 keV is INSIDE the
      forest window [3.3, 5.7].
