S07 -- THE DARK SECTOR'S POWER SPECTRUM: R(k) = 1 (charge, no free
       streaming) vs lambda_fs = 0.558 Mpc (the 5.09 keV particle): the
       reconciliation
============================================================================================================

  THE TWO FACES OF ONE NUMBER (5.09 keV):
    charge face  (G156 ontology, H047 N10): the species IS the scalar's
      charge; lambda_fs = 0 EXACT, R(k) = 1 at EVERY k, no cut; the census
      measures S_meas = 1.0 (N_obs = 19 at the RAR > 1e5 class, G215).
    particle face (G212): m = 5.09 +- 0.10 keV, lambda_fs = 0.5584 Mpc,
      k_hm = 57.22 h/Mpc, M_hm = 7.34e+05 Msun (sim-fit) / 8.41e+06 (window): a WARM
      cut, the sub-halo function inverted below ~1e6 Msun (T^2(1e6) = 5e-13).

  THE CONTRAST, PLAINLY: one sector cannot both free-stream at 0.558 Mpc
  and lock at R(k) = 1.  The particle face IS a suppression --
    k =   10 h/Mpc: T^2 = 0.9704  ->  R = 0.9704  (1 - R = 0.0296)
    k =   30 h/Mpc: T^2 = 0.7074  ->  R = 0.7074  (1 - R = 0.2926)
    k =  100 h/Mpc: T^2 = 0.0162  ->  R = 0.0162  (1 - R = 0.9838)
    k =  300 h/Mpc: T^2 = 0.0000  ->  R = 0.0000  (1 - R = 1.0000)
    -- while the charge face says 1 - R = 0.0000000000 at every one of
    them.  The 5.09 keV number is the equilibrium's phase temperature
    converted to an energy (T_phase = m sigma^2/k_B = T_CMB at z*, G168;
    a temperature does NOT free-stream) OR a rest mass (which does).  The
    contradiction is the ontology of the one number: real for one
    substance, testable for two faces.

  THE COMPOSITE (scale separation): R_comp(k; f_d) = (1 - f_d) + f_d * T^2(k; 5.09)
    plateau: R = 1 - 1.7e-04 at k = 1 h/Mpc (1 - R = 1.7e-04: the charge face,
      the galaxy/cluster/large scales -- the DES-Y3/CMB scales are BLIND to
