      f_d = 0.98: z = -3.45 (the pure relic registered -3.19).
    budget pull: the free dust is ~98% of the dark sector (G234) -> the
      reconciliation is NOT free: the data want a small dust fraction where
      they look; the budget wants a large one.

  THE ONE-PHOTON-SCALE TEST (sees the cut): the Lyman-alpha flux power at
  the scale of ONE absorption (one photon at one velocity width <-> one
  comoving scale, k ~ 5-30 h/Mpc) coincides with the cut's visible onset:
    f_d = 0.5: suppression 1 - R_comp = 0.015 @10 / 0.146 @30 h/Mpc
    f_d = 0.9: suppression 1 - R_comp = 0.027 @10 / 0.263 @30 h/Mpc
    f_d = 1.0: suppression 1 - R_comp = 0.030 @10 / 0.293 @30 h/Mpc
    10% flux-power precision at k ~ 30 sees f_d = 0.9 at ~2.6 sigma and
    f_d = 1 at ~2.9 sigma; the current 95% bound (m > 5.7 keV) already
    sits at this class.

  VERDICTS
  [PASS] V1 THE TWO-FACE STATEMENT: the same sector cannot both free-stream
        at 0.558 Mpc and lock at R(k) = 1 (1-R = 0.29 at 30, 0.98 at 100
        h/Mpc vs the charge's 0.000) -- the contradiction is the ontology
        of the one number, real for one substance, testable for two faces.
  [PASS] V2 THE COMPOSITE P(k) = P_charge + P_dust(smeared): R_comp(k; f_d)
        = (1-f_d) + f_d*T^2(k; 5.09), the plateau at R = 1 (blind to the
        LSS/CMB scales), the break at k ~ 1/lambda_fs, the dust-fraction
        constraint map (forest < 0.76-0.98, census < 0.57-0.85, budget
        pull ~0.98).
  [PASS] V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT: the dark sector's power spectrum is
        RECONCILABLE as a two-component composite at the price of a dust
        fraction the budget and the data pull apart (the composite's own
        tension at budget f_d = -3.45 sigma; pure relic -3.19; census lean
        charge 3.2-4.1 sigma); NOT a contradiction-in-principle, NOT a free
        lunch -- THE K-RANGE THAT DECIDES: the sub-halo decade k ~ 100-500
        h/Mpc (M ~ 1e5-1e8, G156's pre-registration), with the one-photon-
        scale Lyman-alpha flux power at k ~ 10-30 as the auxiliary precision
        test at the cut's visible onset.

